{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_loom", "label": "loom \u2014 a graph runtime for lirbox orchestration skills", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Built parallel to conductor rather than rewriting it: if loom proves out the other three migrate onto its runtime and ~2k lines of fork collapse; if it does not, one skill is lost rather than four."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_fixed_linear_phases_problem", "label": "Problem: conductor executes a fixed linear phase list", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No loop-backs, so every gate hand-rolls a local retry (gateLoop, DoDGate's attempt x round nest with prevUnmetKey/dodStalled, FrontendGate) \u2014 the same idea implemented ~4 times with different escape-hatch semantics; retry is narrow (a fix worker cannot re-enter planning); and the runtime DAG exists only in memory, invisible to a human."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_generator_fork_drift", "label": "Four generators, 2,895 lines, zero shared code", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "scaffold-optimize forked from conductor, scaffold-improve forked from that, scaffold-arena forked again. Every one is loop-shaped and each hand-rolls its own cycle because the backbone cannot express one."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_graph_is_execution_spec", "label": "The graph is the execution spec", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nodes and conditional edges replace PHASES[] and the conductor becomes a small interpreter: retry is an edge, a stall is a visit cap, a fix-loop is a back-edge. gateLoop, the DoDGate nest, dodStalled, prevUnmetKey and FrontendGate's loop are all deleted."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_declarative_edge_predicates", "label": "Declarative edge predicates, never code strings", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Conditions must survive JSON, be editable in the browser UI, and never be eval'd inside the restricted conductor layer. Ordered evaluation: first matching edge wins, 'always' is the fallthrough."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_visit_caps_single_source", "label": "Visit caps live only in invariants.visitCaps", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A '*' default plus per-node overrides gives the validator one authoritative source; nodes carry no visitCap field of their own and the editor writes through to invariants.visitCaps."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_invariants_frozen_at_approval", "label": "Invariants frozen at approval, read from the previous graph", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reading invariants from the submitted graph is a complete bypass: supply mustCross: [] plus an unlocked Implement->terminal edge, the locked fingerprint still matches (that edge is not locked), no dominance check runs, validation returns clean, and every gate is skipped with nothing reported. Only pre-approval may a graph declare its own invariants."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_structural_dominance", "label": "Structural dominance (proof by deletion from start)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Delete gate G; if terminal is still reachable from start, some path avoided it, so G does not dominate \u2014 O(V+E) per gate, position-independent, holds for the whole run."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_positional_dominance", "label": "Positional dominance (from the cursor, over unsatisfied gates)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Required because a back-edge admits start -> DoDGate -> Implement -> terminal: structurally dominated, yet the remaining path never re-crosses the gate that just failed."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_dominance_is_safety_not_sense", "label": "Dominance proves a patch is safe, never that it is sensible", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Visit caps and nodeBudget are the only backstop against a chatty replanner; trace makes every patch auditable."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_preflight_loop", "label": "Pre-flight comment -> replan -> approve loop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Setup and the bootstrap planner run BEFORE human review deliberately \u2014 a graph planned without reading the repo is a guess. The human declares goal and DoD; the loop grounds the decomposition in code before anyone reviews it."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_graph_server", "label": "graph-server.mjs (zero-dep loopback HTTP)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bound to 127.0.0.1, port recorded in state.json. It cannot spawn agents \u2014 agents exist only inside the session \u2014 so replan and approve are a file handoff the skill picks up in a bounded poll loop, and the SKILL freezes the locks, not the server."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_react_flow_editor", "label": "React Flow graph editor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Loaded from CDN (localhost has network; matches flowchart's Mermaid precedent, vendoring is the fallback). Read-only during the run: mid-run comments file to feedback/conductor.jsonl instead of steering, because the moment they steer the overnight property that justifies the skill is gone. Lock badges are a courtesy; the server re-validates every POST."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_one_validator_two_hosts", "label": "One validator module imported by both browser and conductor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same rules and same failure messages on both sides; a second implementation would let UI and runtime disagree about what is legal."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_resume_restores_structure", "label": "Resume must restore structure, not just progress", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The PATCHED graph is persisted, not the approved one \u2014 missing this makes a resumed run silently replay the original topology, the worst bug available in this design. Result keys are <node>#<visit> because a phasesDone set cannot express 'Implement ran three times', and every skip-if-done guard (with its whole bug class) disappears."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_dod_locked_artifacts", "label": "DoD checks as locked artifacts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One mechanism in four parts: hash-lock the checkFile (today the fix worker can edit the test its own check runs, making a weakened check the cheapest route to green); hard-fail baseline-green criteria with a declared green-ok escape hatch; keep checks as committed files so they are reviewable, re-runnable and immune to shell-quoting mangling; and route failure back through real planning instead of a narrow fix worker."}, {"id": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_at_least_once_idempotent_nodes", "label": "At-least-once execution requires idempotent nodes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A crash between runNode and checkpoint re-runs that visit; the re-run may produce a different verdict and take a different edge, which is accepted as more correct than replaying a stale one."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_loom", "target": "readme_loom", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_fixed_linear_phases_problem", "target": "readme_conductor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_fixed_linear_phases_problem", "target": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_loom", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_generator_fork_drift", "target": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_loom", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_generator_fork_drift", "target": "claude_orchestration_loop_skills", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_graph_is_execution_spec", "target": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_loom", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_graph_is_execution_spec", "target": "claude_conductor_layer_purity", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_declarative_edge_predicates", "target": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_graph_is_execution_spec", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_declarative_edge_predicates", "target": "claude_conductor_layer_purity", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_invariants_frozen_at_approval", "target": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_structural_dominance", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_invariants_frozen_at_approval", "target": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_positional_dominance", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_positional_dominance", "target": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_structural_dominance", "relation": "